ices "c7e35bda-557b-58e9-86fc-0850194c1bb0"] [:db/add "1ca97b16-ffef-5260-ac53-9f232f048a0b" :answer-field/correct "245e8010-9f6c-5819-9fdc-92eb0082eb98"] [:db/ensure "1ca97b16-ffef-5260-ac53-9f232f048a0b" :answer-field/validate] [:db/add "301d95a5-2308-57e4-bf5e-65a4471e9fbe" :answer/id #uuid "301d95a5-2308-57e4-bf5e-65a4471e9fbe"] [:db/add "301d95a5-2308-57e4-bf5e-65a4471e9fbe" :answer/type :answer.type/text] [:db/add "301d95a5-2308-57e4-bf5e-65a4471e9fbe" :answer/value "false"] [:db/ensure "301d95a5-2308-57e4-bf5e-65a4471e9fbe" :answer/validate] [:db/add "5b361bb8-6bed-5011-b75c-ba16ec78c708" :answer/id #uuid "5b361bb8-6bed-5011-b75c-ba16ec78c708"] [:db/add "5b361bb8-6bed-5011-b75c-ba16ec78c708" :answer/type :answer.type/text] [:db/add "5b361bb8-6bed-5011-b75c-ba16ec78c708" :answer/value "true"] [:db/ensure "5b361bb8-6bed-5011-b75c-ba16ec78c708" :answer/validate] [:db/add "bd3f9fe6-6b7a-515a-a778-d87f1c1495ba" :answer-field/id #uuid "bd3f9fe6-6b7a-515a-a778-d87f1c1495ba"] [:db/add "bd3f9fe6-6b7a-515a-a778-d87f1c1495ba" :answer-field/key "None of the above"] [:db/add "bd3f9fe6-6b7a-515a-a778-d87f1c1495ba" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/checkbox] [:db/add "bd3f9fe6-6b7a-515a-a778-d87f1c1495ba" :answer-field/choices "301d95a5-2308-57e4-bf5e-65a4471e9fbe"] [:db/add "bd3f9fe6-6b7a-515a-a778-d87f1c1495ba" :answer-field/choices "5b361bb8-6bed-5011-b75c-ba16ec78c708"] [:db/add "bd3f9fe6-6b7a-515a-a778-d87f1c1495ba" :answer-field/correct "301d95a5-2308-57e4-bf5e-65a4471e9fbe"] [:db/ensure "bd3f9fe6-6b7a-515a-a778-d87f1c1495ba" :answer-field/validate] [:db/add "954937f1-7726-5be2-9cf2-ace75716eea5" :question/id #uuid "954937f1-7726-5be2-9cf2-ace75716eea5"] [:db/add "954937f1-7726-5be2-9cf2-ace75716eea5" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-2xy$ and its slope field. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply."] [:db/add "954937f1-7726-5be2-9cf2-ace75716eea5" :question/worked-solution "First, we define $f(x,y)=-2xy.$ Then, our differential equation is $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y).$ \n\nNotice that $f(x,y)=0$ when $x=0$ or $y=0.$ The lines $x=0$ and $y=0$ divide the plane into the usual four quadrants.\n\nIf we compute the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each quadrant (by considering some test points, for example), we get the following:\n\n![](images/2c/2c218c7df2bf4e159b4bffaccb4296beab8e3f44ab82d56b3589050af92ccf8e.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement “At every point in the third quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative” is true. If $(x,y)$ is in the third quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)<0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is negative for any point $(x,y)$ in the third quadrant.\n\n- Statement “At every point in the second quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative” is false. If $(x,y)$ is in the second quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in the second quadrant.\n\n- Statement “At every point in the fourth quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative” is false. If $(x,y)$ is in the fourth quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in the fourth quadrant.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “At every point in the third quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative” only."] [:db/add "954937f1-7726-5be2-9cf2-ace75716eea5" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] [:db/add "954937f1-7726-5be2-9cf2-ace75716eea5" :question/answer-fields "82593be4-c604-5fda-8b67-14710334e756"] [:db/add "954937f1-7726-5be2-9cf2-ace75716eea5" :question/answer-fields "71ebc04d-0aa8-567a-8462-97edb6e92033"] [:db/