ces "d1484a87-e37c-53a4-8a20-887bc62c7c02"] [:db/add "3eda00a6-2b53-5eb5-9443-bc481456b9ea" :answer-field/choices "45a95f97-a1c7-5408-8e45-38520c0e9deb"] [:db/add "3eda00a6-2b53-5eb5-9443-bc481456b9ea" :answer-field/correct "d1484a87-e37c-53a4-8a20-887bc62c7c02"] [:db/ensure "3eda00a6-2b53-5eb5-9443-bc481456b9ea" :answer-field/validate] [:db/add "1345f069-f11b-56fe-958c-de725b58eb1f" :question/id #uuid "1345f069-f11b-56fe-958c-de725b58eb1f"] [:db/add "1345f069-f11b-56fe-958c-de725b58eb1f" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-6xy$ and its slope field. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply."] [:db/add "1345f069-f11b-56fe-958c-de725b58eb1f" :question/worked-solution "First, we define $f(x,y)=-6xy.$ Then, our differential equation is $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y).$ \n\nNotice that $f(x,y)=0$ when $x=0$ or $y=0.$ The lines $x=0$ and $y=0$ divide the plane into the usual four quadrants.\n\nIf we compute the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each quadrant (by considering some test points, for example), we get the following:\n\n![](images/2c/2c218c7df2bf4e159b4bffaccb4296beab8e3f44ab82d56b3589050af92ccf8e.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement “At every point in the second quadrant, the slope of the slope field is positive” is true. If $(x,y)$ is in the second quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in the second quadrant.\n\n- Statement “At every point in the first quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative” is true. If $(x,y)$ is in the first quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)<0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is negative for any point $(x,y)$ in the first quadrant.\n\n- Statement “At every point in the fourth quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative” is false. If $(x,y)$ is in the fourth quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in the fourth quadrant.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “At every point in the second quadrant, the slope of the slope field is positive”; “At every point in the first quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative”."] [:db/add "1345f069-f11b-56fe-958c-de725b58eb1f" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] [:db/add "1345f069-f11b-56fe-958c-de725b58eb1f" :question/answer-fields "e4b661b9-6e36-5c48-b27d-843339c86705"] [:db/add "1345f069-f11b-56fe-958c-de725b58eb1f" :question/answer-fields "79aad520-644b-54cf-9059-eada322e4888"] [:db/add "1345f069-f11b-56fe-958c-de725b58eb1f" :question/answer-fields "e9bfb2b5-5172-5ec8-9973-6fe90c04f85e"] [:db/add "1345f069-f11b-56fe-958c-de725b58eb1f" :question/answer-fields "3eda00a6-2b53-5eb5-9443-bc481456b9ea"] [:db/ensure "1345f069-f11b-56fe-958c-de725b58eb1f" :question/validate] [:db/add 17592186172039 :knowledge-point/questions "1345f069-f11b-56fe-958c-de725b58eb1f"] [:db/add "8e31e2a6-5a9c-59e5-b656-53e1849a4c55" :answer/id #uuid "8e31e2a6-5a9c-59e5-b656-53e1849a4c55"] [:db/add "8e31e2a6-5a9c-59e5-b656-53e1849a4c55" :answer/type :answer.type/text] [:db/add "8e31e2a6-5a9c-59e5-b656-53e1849a4c55" :answer/value "false"] [:db/ensure "8e31e2a6-5a9c-59e5-b656-53e1849a4c55" :answer/validate] [:db/add "8d5d9307-e136-5c27-906a-06fae418a476" :answer/id #uuid "8d5d9307-e136-5c27-906a-06fae418a476"] [:db/add "8d5d9307-e136-5c27-906a-06fae418a476" :answer/type :answer.type/text] [:db/add "8d5d9307-e136-5c27-906a-06fae418a476" :answer/value "true"] [:db/ensure "8d5d9307-e136-5c27-906a-06fae418a476" :answer/validate] [:db/add "6d6ed8a6-7d75-5550-8a8c-2db9c82f28df" :answer-field/id #uuid "6d6ed8a6-7d75-5550-8a8c-2db9c82f28df"] [:db/add "6d6ed8a6-7d