6"] [:db/add "e61cbeb9-6f77-5f4e-86af-43c701736476" :answer/type :answer.type/text] [:db/add "e61cbeb9-6f77-5f4e-86af-43c701736476" :answer/value "false"] [:db/ensure "e61cbeb9-6f77-5f4e-86af-43c701736476" :answer/validate] [:db/add "6dbbdf50-4bc2-502e-9cfd-c889652b44b1" :answer/id #uuid "6dbbdf50-4bc2-502e-9cfd-c889652b44b1"] [:db/add "6dbbdf50-4bc2-502e-9cfd-c889652b44b1" :answer/type :answer.type/text] [:db/add "6dbbdf50-4bc2-502e-9cfd-c889652b44b1" :answer/value "true"] [:db/ensure "6dbbdf50-4bc2-502e-9cfd-c889652b44b1" :answer/validate] [:db/add "6544f083-6a49-585b-9750-d235f087c4e7" :answer-field/id #uuid "6544f083-6a49-585b-9750-d235f087c4e7"] [:db/add "6544f083-6a49-585b-9750-d235f087c4e7" :answer-field/key "None of the above"] [:db/add "6544f083-6a49-585b-9750-d235f087c4e7" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/checkbox] [:db/add "6544f083-6a49-585b-9750-d235f087c4e7" :answer-field/choices "e61cbeb9-6f77-5f4e-86af-43c701736476"] [:db/add "6544f083-6a49-585b-9750-d235f087c4e7" :answer-field/choices "6dbbdf50-4bc2-502e-9cfd-c889652b44b1"] [:db/add "6544f083-6a49-585b-9750-d235f087c4e7" :answer-field/correct "e61cbeb9-6f77-5f4e-86af-43c701736476"] [:db/ensure "6544f083-6a49-585b-9750-d235f087c4e7" :answer-field/validate] [:db/add "764de3d1-5894-55be-8e26-0caf40d3c432" :question/id #uuid "764de3d1-5894-55be-8e26-0caf40d3c432"] [:db/add "764de3d1-5894-55be-8e26-0caf40d3c432" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-2xy$ and its slope field. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply."] [:db/add "764de3d1-5894-55be-8e26-0caf40d3c432" :question/worked-solution "First, we define $f(x,y)=-2xy.$ Then, our differential equation is $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y).$ \n\nNotice that $f(x,y)=0$ when $x=0$ or $y=0.$ The lines $x=0$ and $y=0$ divide the plane into the usual four quadrants.\n\nIf we compute the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each quadrant (by considering some test points, for example), we get the following:\n\n![](images/2c/2c218c7df2bf4e159b4bffaccb4296beab8e3f44ab82d56b3589050af92ccf8e.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement “At every point in the fourth quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative” is false. If $(x,y)$ is in the fourth quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in the fourth quadrant.\n\n- Statement “At every point in the third quadrant, the slope of the slope field is positive” is false. If $(x,y)$ is in the third quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)<0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is negative for any point $(x,y)$ in the third quadrant.\n\n- Statement “At every point in the second quadrant, the slope of the slope field is positive” is true. If $(x,y)$ is in the second quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in the second quadrant.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “At every point in the second quadrant, the slope of the slope field is positive” only."] [:db/add "764de3d1-5894-55be-8e26-0caf40d3c432" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] [:db/add "764de3d1-5894-55be-8e26-0caf40d3c432" :question/answer-fields "86f5078b-71ac-572a-803e-18ae809816f3"] [:db/add "764de3d1-5894-55be-8e26-0caf40d3c432" :question/answer-fields "a4d45b94-b0e8-5c09-baa0-33a750b24587"] [:db/add "764de3d1-5894-55be-8e26-0caf40d3c432" :question/answer-fields "36a3dbcf-8363-569d-aad7-f87855406f76"] [:db/add "764de3d1-5894-55be-8e26-0caf40d3c432" :question/answer-fields "6544f083-6a49-585b-9750-d235f087c4e7"] [:db/ensure "764de3d1-5894-55be-8e26-0caf40d3c432" :question/validate] [:db/add 17592186172039 :knowledge-point